    {
      "title": "CommonJS vs ES Modules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CommonJS vs ES Modules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Loading model",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CommonJS",
                "ESM"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Syntax",
                  "`require()` / `module.exports`",
                  "`import` / `export`"
                ],
                [
                  "Loading",
                  "sync, whole file runs at the call, cached in `require.cache`",
                  "parsed first, async"
                ],
                [
                  "Position",
                  "anywhere, computed path",
                  "hoisted, literal string"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Conditional load: `import('./x.js')` returns a ==Promise=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which system per file",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`.mjs` always {green:ESM}, `.cjs` always {orange:CJS}",
                "`.js` + `\"type\": \"module\"` in nearest package.json = ESM",
                "`.js` default (`\"commonjs\"`) = CJS"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and gotchas",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "const fs = require('fs');",
                "module.exports = { run };"
              ],
              "note": "CJS"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "import fs from 'fs';",
                "export const run = () => {};"
              ],
              "note": "ESM"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Relative imports need the extension: `./util.js`",
                "No `__dirname` or `require`: use `import.meta.url` or `import.meta.dirname`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**require() an ES module?** Older Node loads sync, ESM is async; `import()` returns a Promise",
                "**CJS or ESM?** Extension, then nearest `type`",
                "**Copies vs live bindings?** CJS copies values; ESM sees later changes"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "package.json Essentials",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "package.json Essentials",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Identity and Entry",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`name` + `version` required to publish; name ==lowercase==, no spaces",
                "`private: true` blocks accidental `npm publish`",
                "`main`: the **CJS** entry file",
                "`\"type\": \"module\"`: .js files become ==ESM==",
                "`exports`: maps subpaths and `import`/`require`; unlisted deep imports blocked; **beats** `main`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Starter File",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`npm init -y` = defaults; `npm init` asks questions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{",
                "  \"name\": \"app\",",
                "  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",",
                "  \"type\": \"module\",",
                "  \"scripts\": { \"start\": \"node index.js\" }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Trailing comma or comment: ==strict JSON== breaks",
                "`Cannot use import statement outside a module`: older Node or `\"type\": \"commonjs\"`",
                "Node 22.7+ runs typeless ESM with a warning; still add `\"type\": \"module\"`",
                "Hand edit without `npm install`: lockfile out of sync"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**main/module/exports?** `main` CJS entry; `module` bundler-only hint; `exports` ==wins==",
                "**`\"type\": \"module\"`?** .js parsed as ESM",
                "**private: true?** stops accidental publish of an app"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "dependencies vs devDependencies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "dependencies vs devDependencies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Runtime vs Build",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "dependencies",
                "devDependencies"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Needed for",
                  "runtime in production (express, react)",
                  "build, test, lint (jest, eslint, typescript, vite)"
                ],
                [
                  "Install",
                  "`npm i pkg`",
                  "`npm i -D pkg`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What a Production Install Skips",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`npm install --omit=dev` skips ==devDependencies==",
                "Older flag: `--production`; `NODE_ENV=production` does the same",
                "Installing your library gets its ==dependencies== only, never its devDependencies"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Other Dependency Kinds",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`peerDependencies`",
                  "the **host app** must supply it (a React plugin needs react); auto-installed since npm 7"
                ],
                [
                  "`optionalDependencies`",
                  "may fail to install without breaking the install"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`dependencies`: what you ==import==",
                "`peerDependencies`: what you ==share== with the host"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`typescript` in devDependencies but compiled on deploy: the production install omits it, the build fails",
                "Test libraries in dependencies: bloated images and installs"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Semver and Lockfiles",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Semver and Lockfiles",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Semver and Ranges",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH==, e.g. `2.4.1`",
                "{green:PATCH}: bug fix",
                "{blue:MINOR}: backward-compatible feature",
                "{red:MAJOR}: breaking change"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Range",
                "Allows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`^1.2.3`",
                  "1.x.x at or above 1.2.3 (default)"
                ],
                [
                  "`~1.2.3`",
                  "1.2.x only"
                ],
                [
                  "`1.2.3`",
                  "exact"
                ],
                [
                  "`^0.2.3`",
                  "0.2.x only: 0.x may break"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Lockfile",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`package-lock.json` pins exact version, tarball URL, ==integrity hash==",
                "Covers the whole tree, incl. transitive deps",
                "==Commit it=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Behaviour"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`npm install`",
                  "respects lock, may update it"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm ci`",
                  "strictly from lock, wipes `node_modules`, fails on mismatch: use in ==CI=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Deleting the lockfile or committing two (npm + yarn): each machine gets other versions",
                "Never hand-edit the lockfile"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`npm outdated` shows what can change",
                "`npm update` moves within ranges"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**^ vs ~?** `^` keeps the major, `~` keeps the minor",
                "**Commit the lock? npm ci?** Same tree everywhere; `ci` is strict and clean, `install` may update",
                "**Semver limit?** Promises compatibility per bump, but maintainers can mislabel breaking changes"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "npm Scripts and Everyday Commands",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "npm Scripts and Everyday Commands",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Scripts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`npm run <name>` runs a script; ==test==, ==start==, `stop` skip `run`",
                "==node_modules/.bin== is on the **PATH** during a script",
                "So `\"lint\": \"eslint .\"` needs no global install"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Hooks and Arguments",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Hook",
                "Runs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`pretest`, `postbuild`",
                  "automatically before / after that script"
                ],
                [
                  "`prepare`",
                  "after local `npm install`, before publish"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`prepare` is the place to build or install ==git hooks==",
                "Everything after ==--== is forwarded to the script",
                "`&&` chains steps: each must succeed (`tsc && node dist`)",
                "`npx <tool>` runs a binary without a permanent install"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "npm run test -- --watch",
                "npx eslint ."
              ],
              "note": "-- forwards --watch to the test script"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Everyday Commands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`npm install`",
                  "install everything"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm i pkg`",
                  "add a dependency"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm i -D pkg`",
                  "add a devDependency"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm uninstall pkg`",
                  "remove it"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm ls`",
                  "show the tree"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm outdated`",
                  "show newer versions"
                ],
                [
                  "`npm update`",
                  "update within ranges"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Global `-g` tools cause {red:version drift}",
                "`rm -rf` in scripts breaks **Windows** teammates",
                "Forgetting `--` before forwarded flags"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Modules and npm",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Modules and npm",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Modules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CJS",
                "ESM"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Syntax",
                  "`require`, `module.exports`",
                  "`import`, `export`"
                ],
                [
                  "Load",
                  "sync, dynamic",
                  "static, async"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs",
                  "default for `.js`",
                  "`\"type\": \"module\"` or `.mjs`"
                ],
                [
                  "Relative path",
                  "no extension",
                  "==extension required=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "CJS loads ESM: `import()`, or `require()` on Node 22.12+/20.19+ (no top-level await)",
                "ESM loads CJS: default import"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. npm",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "dependencies",
                  "runtime"
                ],
                [
                  "devDependencies",
                  "build, test (`-D`)"
                ],
                [
                  "peerDependencies",
                  "host app supplies it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`npm i --omit=dev` skips dev deps",
                "`^` same major (default), `~` same minor, none = exact",
                "`^0.2.3` = 0.2.x only",
                "`npm run <name>`, `test`/`start` shortcut, `pre`/`post` hooks, args after `--`",
                ".bin on PATH; `npx` runs one-off tools"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Lockfile",
              "text": "Commit it, never hand-edit. `npm ci` in CI, `npm install` locally."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fix-it list",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Cannot use import statement`: add `\"type\": \"module\"` or `.mjs` (older Node)",
                "`require`/`__dirname` not defined: in ESM, use `import()`, `import.meta`",
                "`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`: missing file extension",
                "`npm ci` lock mismatch: `npm install`, commit lock"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A file `app.mjs` runs `console.log(__dirname)`. What happens, and what replaces it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`ReferenceError`: ESM has no `__dirname`.",
                "Use `import.meta.dirname`, or derive it from `import.meta.url`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "package.json says `^0.2.3`. The registry has 0.2.9, 0.3.0 and 1.0.0. Which version installs?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`0.2.9`.",
                "Below 1.0.0, ^ pins the minor, because a minor bump may break."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A Dockerfile runs `npm ci --omit=dev`, then `npm run build`, which calls tsc. typescript is a devDependency. What breaks?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`tsc` was never installed, so the build fails.",
                "Build before omitting dev packages, or use a multi-stage build."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
